1. {d}en-lil₂ su₃-ra₂-še₃ dug₄-ga-ni mah (1:inim-ma-ni:1) kug-ga-am₃
#tr.en: @wDN{Enlil's} commands are by far the loftiest,
#lem: Enlil[1]DN; sud[distant]; dug[speak]; mah[great]; inim[word]; kug[pure]
#etcsl: line-id=1

:1v.1.1: ($1 ms. has instead:$) dug₄-ga-ni
#lem: dug[speak]

#etcsl#cite Cited in OB catalogue from Nibru, at Philadelphia, 0.2.01, line 5; OB catalogue in the Louvre, 0.2.02, line 5; OB catalogue from Urim (U2), 0.2.04, line 16; OB catalogue at Andrews University, 0.2.11, line 10

2. niŋ₂ nu-kur₂-ru ka-ta e₃-a-ni nam ul-še₃ tar-re
#tr.en: his @varh[t4051.v1]{words } @vart[t4051.v2,t4051.v1]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} commands } are holy, his utterances are immutable!
#lem: niŋ[thing]; kur[different]; kag[mouth]; e[leave]; nam[fate]; ul[distant time]; tar[cut]
#etcsl: line-id=2

3. igi il₂-la-ni kur-re di-di
#tr.en: The fate he decides is everlasting, his glance makes the mountains anxious,
#lem: igi[eye]; il[raise]; kur[mountain(s)]; di[speak]
#etcsl: line-id=3

4. ŋiš-nu₁₁ il₂-la-ni kur-šag₄-ga igi ŋal₂
#tr.en: his …… reaches (?) into the interior of the mountains.
#lem: ŋešnu[light]; il[raise]; kuršag[center of the mountains]; igi[eye]; ŋal[⟦be⟧ to be (there]
#etcsl: line-id=4

5. a-a {d}en-lil₂ barag kug (1:barag:1) mah-a daŋal-bi tuš-a-ni
#tr.en: All the gods of the earth bow down to Father @wDN{Enlil},
